# Architecture Rules

## Nest

- Controllers: HTTP + DTO validation only
- Services: business logic and orchestration
- Provide shared services once; **export** from owning module (e.g. S3 metadata)
- Avoid `common/types` importing TypeORM entities (cycle risk)
- Config via `src/config/` — no new scattered `process.env` in feature code
- Global `ValidationPipe` in `main.ts`

## Lambda

- Keep code under `lambda/` only
- Do not import Nest `src/`
- Structured logs; no full SQS/S3 payload dumps

## CloudFormation

- Use `ImportValue` for `aws-infra-*` networking
- Env-specific DB/TG/IAM imports must match `Environment` (no prod→dev hardcoding)
- Never paste foreign VPC/subnet IDs from other projects

## MUST NOT

- Duplicate Nest providers across modules instead of exporting
- Cross-import Nest ↔ Lambda source trees
- Hardcode RDS hostnames in npm scripts (use env)
